% A DESCENDANT directory's self.glp redefines a type name this one defines, and
% this program's OWN modules must keep THIS definition: the module system has the
% nearer definition shadow the farther FOR THE MODULES OF ITS SUBTREE, and
% `inner/` is not this directory's subtree scope but its own.  The linked program
% used to hold one flat type namespace, so whichever `Lot` the directory walk
% reached first became every module's `Lot` — reported by Currencies Code on
% 2026-09-03, where `txn.glp` was checked against `coins/self.glp`'s `Lot` and
% the program did not load.  GREEN, and green whichever order the walk takes.
Lot ::= lot(Constant, Constant, Constant).
imported procedure txn#select(Lot?, Constant).
exported procedure go(Lot?, Constant).
go(L, C?) :- txn # select(L?, C).
